        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "07808828-ef76-5ad9-b17d-5c30a1879337",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Works: Sons and Lovers (1981 TV serial), Sons and Lovers\n- Organizations: BBC\n- People: D. H. Lawrence, Eileen Atkins, Tom Bell, Karl Johnson, Lynn Dearth, Leonie Mellinger\n- Roles: actress, screenwriter\n- Awards: Olivier Award\n\nFacts:\n- D. H. Lawrence wrote the book \"Sons and Lovers,\" which was adapted into the 1981 BBC television serial \"Sons and Lovers.\"\n- The 1981 BBC television serial \"Sons and Lovers\" starred Eileen Atkins, Tom Bell, Karl Johnson, Lynn Dearth, and Leonie Mellinger.\n- Eileen Atkins was born on 16 June 1934 and is an English actress and occasional screenwriter.\n- Eileen Atkins won the Olivier Award for Best Supporting Performance in 1988 for multiple roles.\n- Eileen Atkins won the Olivier Award for Best Actress for \"The Unexpected Man\" in 1999.\n- Eileen Atkins won the Olivier Award for Best Actress for \"Honour\" in 2004.\n- Eileen Atkins is a three-time Olivier Award winner.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
